  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1511.03692v1</id>
    <title>Optimal bounds for convergence of expected spectral distributions to the semi-circular law for the $4+ε$ moment ensemble</title>
    <updated>2015-11-11T21:31:50Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.03692v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1511.03692v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>This paper extends a previous bound of order $O(n^{-1})$ of the authors (arXiv:1405.7820[math.PR]), for the rate of convergence in Kolmogorov distance of the expected spectral distribution of a Wigner random matrix ensemble to the semicircular law. Here we relax the moment conditions for entries of the Wigner matrices from order $8$ to order $4+ ε$ for an arbitrary small $ε&gt;0$.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2015-11-11T21:31:50Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>This paper is an addendum to arXiv:1405.7820 , relaxing moment conditions in Theorem 1.3 of that paper to order $4+ε$. For a discussion of the relevant literature we refer to the previous paper arXiv:1405.7820 (to appear Probab. Theory Relat. Fields (2015+))</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.PR"/>
